  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong dark-console identity, disciplined cyan/red/green semantics, and a clear desktop hero-to-artifact hierarchy. However, tablet and especially mobile become extremely tall, dense scans with undersized mono labels and weak row differentiation; the mobile table collapses into repetitive card-like stacks without enough visual rhythm. The desktop header’s oversized clipped ghost lettering distracts, while tablet/mobile navigation feels crowded and visibly truncates “LIVE WIRE.”",
    "fix": "Increase small-text sizes and contrast, tighten the mobile transaction rows, and add stronger grouping/dividers to improve scan rhythm. Replace the clipped header backdrop with a quieter active-state treatment, and make compact navigation show the current section clearly instead of truncating it.",
